 conformer in amyloid disease?</article-title><source>Acc Chem Res</source><volume>39</volume><fpage>594</fpage><lpage>602</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16981675</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050134-b040"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jarrett</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Lansbury</surname><given-names>PT</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Seeding &#x0201c;one-dimensional crystallization&#x0201d; of amyloid: A pathogenic mechanism in Alzheimer's disease and scrapie?</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>1055</fpage><lpage>1058</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8513491</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050134-b041"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Serio</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cashikar</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Kowal</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sawicki</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Moslehi</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Nucleated conformational conversion and the replication of conformational information by a prion determinant</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>289</volume><fpage>1317</fpage><lpage>1321</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10958771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050134-b042"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Librizzi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Rischel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The kinetic behavior of insulin fibrillation is determined by heterogeneous nucleation pathways</article-title><source>Protein Sci</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>3129</fpag